From: environment_builder
Subject: [PATCH] configs: kr260-omnv: the KV260 root cell's memory layout, no FPGA base design

The fork's KR260 Omnivisor root cell ("simple configuration for Kria kr260")
is its KV260 root cell with two differences, both of which stop it:

- the hypervisor's memory at 0x7e000000, where the root cell's two ivshmem
  regions are (JAILHOUSE_SHMEM_NET_REGIONS at 0x7e000000 and 0x7e100000):
  the KV260 root cell has it at 0x7f000000, the second half of the 32 MB
  jailhouse@7e000000 reservation of the DT, which is where it goes here too,
  with 15 MB instead of 16: the K26 SOM's DT reserves pmu@7ff00000 (1 MB)
  for the PMU firmware, which the KV260 root cell's last megabyte overlaps;
- the FPGA base design "system.bit" ("to do"): the driver loads the named
  bitstream into the FPGA at "jailhouse enable" and fails without it. The
  Omnivisor has no DFX design for the KR260, so the name is empty, which the
  driver skips (driver/main.c).

The KR260 has the same K26 SOM as the KV260 (DDR, R5 cores, UART1), and the
root cell's MMIO regions already cover the KR260's carrier devices (GEM0,
GEM1, both USB controllers): the rest of the configuration is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/configs/arm64/zynqmp-kr260-omnv.c b/configs/arm64/zynqmp-kr260-omnv.c
index 0f7ea39e..11d8cf9a 100755
--- a/configs/arm64/zynqmp-kr260-omnv.c
+++ b/configs/arm64/zynqmp-kr260-omnv.c
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
  *		ranges;
  *		jailhouse_reserved: jailhouse@7e000000 {
  *			no-map;
- *			reg = <0x0 0x7e000000 0x0 0x1000000>;
+ *			reg = <0x0 0x7e000000 0x0 0x2000000>;
  *		}; 
  *	};
  */
@@ -46,8 +46,10 @@ struct {
 		.architecture = JAILHOUSE_ARM64,
 		.flags = JAILHOUSE_SYS_VIRTUAL_DEBUG_CONSOLE,
 		.hypervisor_memory = {
-			.phys_start = 0x7e000000,
-			.size =       0x01000000,
+			/* above the ivshmem regions at 0x7e000000, as on the KV260,
+			 * below the PMU firmware's pmu@7ff00000 (K26 SOM DT) */
+			.phys_start = 0x7f000000,
+			.size =       0x00f00000,
 		},
 		.debug_console = {
 			.address = 0xff010000,
@@ -106,7 +108,8 @@ struct {
 				.nic_size = 0x100000,
 			},
 			.fpga = {
-				.fpga_base_bitstream = "system.bit", 	    // to do ....
+				/* no DFX design for the KR260: no base design at enable */
+				.fpga_base_bitstream = "",
 				.fpga_base_addr = 0x80000000,				// FPGA base address
 				.fpga_flags = JAILHOUSE_FPGA_FULL, 			// flags for the FPGA base
 				.fpga_max_regions = 3,						// there will be 3 reconfigurable regions
